  "dimensions": [
    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_a5866744",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: lizzie_velasquez_was_born_with_a_rare_disease_and_is_now_a_motivational_speaker; hasOverallIntent: Harmful; overall-intent-description: The image depicts Lizzie Velasquez, a woman with a rare genetic condition causing extreme physical differences, with text stating she was born with a rare disease and is now a motivational speaker. The overall intent is to present her as an inspirational figure overcoming adversity. However, the meme's framing can be harmful because it implicitly or explicitly relies on the 'inspiration porn' trope — portraying her as an object of pity or admiration for her perceived 'overcoming' of her condition, rather than focusing on her agency, achievements, or humanity. This can be seen as a form of ableism, as it reduces her to a symbol of inspiration for others' suffering, potentially reinforcing societal stigma around physical difference and implying her value is derived solely from her resilience rather than her individuality. The meme may unintentionally or intentionally normalize the idea that people with disabilities are only worthy or interesting when they are 'inspiring,' which can be demeaning and harmful to the disability community.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_83397408"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
    },
    {
